==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{sense|spin}} {{alter|en|English||US|id=spin}}
* {{sense|render into English}} {{alter|en|English||dated|rare|id=render into English}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=spin|:from<unc>|English}}
{{unc|en}}. It is speculated to relate either to people from England introducing the technique for billiards or bowling in the United States, or perhaps from a particular person with the surname ''English''.<ref name="OED">{{R:OED Online|entry=English|code=62251|subid=5417073|date=December 2008}}</ref>

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɪŋ.ɡlɪʃ/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-english.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-uk-English.oga|a=UK}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪŋɡlɪʃ|s=2}}
* {{hmp|en|English}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{senseid|en|spin}} {{lb|en|uncountable|North American}} [[spinning|Spinning]] or [[rotary]] [[motion]] given to a [[ball]] around the vertical [[axis]], as in [[pool]], [[billiards]] or [[bowling]]; [[spin]], [[sidespin]].
#: {{ux|en|You can't hit it directly, but maybe if you give it some '''english'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=S. Moran|title=Bronx Boy: Book One of The Zombie Island Trilogy|page=179
|passage=There was a magical way of putting '''English''' on the dice to result in a six.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension|figurative}} An unusual or unexpected [[interpretation]] of a text or idea, a [[spin]], a [[nuance]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1993|author=Thomas Cripps|title=Making Movies Black|page=94|text=Preston Sturgis in his ''Sullivan’s Travels'' (1942) put some '''english''' on the idea in a bit about a filthy, defeated, ''white'' chaingang that is invited to a rural black church for an evening of old movies.|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=ypXaryjPaV0C&pg=PA94}}

